      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "last two lines may be thus rendered. “ Therefore these very",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "poor insignificant people might or might not give anything.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "[There is nothing wonderful in that.] But fie on those &c.”—",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXVII.—गायनाः = singers. Pâṇini III., 1, 147. This form of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the word also occurs in the Naishadhîya I., 103 and in the Râmâ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "yaṇa ; but I have mislaid the latter reference. The commentator",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "says नेति नामेति संबोधने. Râmarshi says निश्चितं संबोधने वा. See note on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Misc. St. 1, Nîtis'ataka. Râmarshi says एतेन राजकुलस्य पापरूपत्वाद्ध-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "यमयोग्या इत्यर्थः. The following lines of Juvenal may be compared :",
          "end": "line"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "“ What’s Rome to me, what business have I there,",
          "end": "line"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "I who can neither lie nor falsely swear,",
          "end": "line"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Nor praise my patron’s undeserving rhymes” &c. (Ancient clas-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "sics for English readers p. 73.) The implication is that those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "persons only who can descend to such occupations find enter-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "tainment in the royal household.—Vaitâlîya.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXVIII.—हति = destruction. It occurs again in St. 30, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "in other places also. The idea is that in the first instance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "learning was a means to the destruction of worldly troubles,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "afterwards to the achievement of worldly pleasures, and now",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "lastly receiving no appreciation at all, it is departing from the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "earth. For the last, St. 2 may be compared. सापि i. e. even in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "this lowest condition.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXIX.—कोपि = some great person. Comp. किमपि indescrib-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "able. वदान्यानां जितेंद्रियाणां सत्यसंधानां शूराणां च युद्धे निहतानां शिरांसि श्रीमहादेवः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "शिरसि बिभर्तीत्यागमः (Râmarshi). नृभिर्नमद्भिः is noticeable. It is equiva-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "lent to नृणां नमनैः. “ Why should there be this......in consequence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of—?” प्रवण = strongly bent on.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXX.—अर्थानाम्. Siddh. Kaum. I., 297. यावत् = साकल्येन (Râ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "marshi.) इत्थम् = अमुना प्रकारेण according to the commentators who",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
